## Rule SF-1 — Tiered Line Budget

Agent-facing skill files are subject to tiered line-count ceilings, adopted from gsd
v1.37.0 (issue #2361) and applied to the canonical 14-file set listed in
`scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py::MIRRORED_FILES`:

| Tier    | Ceiling | Files                                                | Enforced by |
|---------|---------|-------------------------------------------------------|---|
| Default | < 500   | `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`                      | `tests/test_integration.py::test_skill_md_under_500_lines` |
| Large   | ≤ 1000  | `workflow-system/agent/references/*.md` (10 files)    | `tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py::test_reference_within_large_tier` |
| XL      | ≤ 1600  | `workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md` (3 files)       | `tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py::test_example_within_xl_tier` |

Rationale: SKILL.md is loaded into every dispatcher prompt and must stay tight;
references are loaded on-demand by L1/L2/L3 agents and may carry richer context;
examples are only consulted when an agent needs a worked trace, so they get the
widest budget.

Verify before committing changes with either:

```bash
wc -l workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md \
      workflow-system/agent/references/*.md \
      workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md
python -m pytest tests/test_integration.py::test_skill_md_under_500_lines \
                 tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py -v
```

## Rule SF-2 — Required Frontmatter Keys

SKILL.md frontmatter (YAML between `---` delimiters) must include ALL of: `id`, `version`, `purpose`, `triggers`, `tier`, `token_estimate`, `last_updated`, `name`, `description`. The `description` field must describe WHEN/WHY to activate the skill (trigger conditions), not WHAT the skill does (capability summary). This prevents agents from using the description as a compressed substitute for reading the full skill content.

## Rule SF-3 — Version Consistency

The version string must match `src/devolaflow/__init__.py` `__version__` in ALL of these tracked locations:

**Canonical 7 (the ones `scripts/bump_version.py` pattern-replaces — tracked, required):**

1. SKILL.md frontmatter `version:`, banner, and body "Current version:" text (file: `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`)
2. `workflow-skill.yaml` identity section
3. `pyproject.toml` version field
4. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py` SOURCE_VERSION
5. `tests/test_smoke.py` version assertion
6. `README.md` badge and version example
7. `workflow-system/human/demo/benchmark-results/index.html` SAMPLE_DATA version

**Project-local opt-in mirror (NOT tracked — gitignored as of chore/cursor-skill-mirror-untrack):**

The `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/` directory is the project-local Cursor skill bundle. It is identical to what `scripts/install.sh::install_cursor` produces — devs who want the DevolaFlow skill auto-loaded while working in *this* repo can opt in with:

```bash
python scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py --init   # create mirror from canonical (one-time)
make sync-cursor-skill                        # refresh existing mirror
make check-cursor-skill                       # exits 0 if mirror absent OR in sync; 1 only on drift
```

Bytewise parity is enforced **only when the mirror is present locally**:

- `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/SKILL.md` ↔ `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`
- `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/references/*.md` (10 files) ↔ `workflow-system/agent/references/*.md`
- `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/examples/*.md` (3 files) ↔ `workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md`
- `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/.devola-flow-version` first line == `__version__`

`scripts/bump_version.py` invokes `scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py` automatically after every bump; the sync script is a no-op when the mirror directory doesn't exist, so CI and fresh clones pass without it. The `tests/test_version.py` mirror-parity assertions skip themselves when the mirror is absent.

**Workflow:**

```bash
python scripts/bump_version.py <new-version>   # bumps canonical 7 + auto-syncs mirror IFF present
make sync-human-docs                            # regenerate EN/ZH human docs
python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v       # asserts canonical 7; mirror tests skip if absent
```

If you locally edit `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` or any reference/example outside of a version bump and you have the mirror locally installed, run `make sync-cursor-skill` before committing canonical changes.

## Rule SF-4 — Valid Reference Links

Every `references/xxx.md` path mentioned in SKILL.md must correspond to an actual file under `workflow-system/agent/references/`. Do not reference files that do not exist.

Current valid references: `agent-hierarchy.md`, `agent-workspace.md`, `behavioral-guidelines.md`, `context-isolation.md`, `decomposition-gate.md`, `execution-protocol.md`, `message-schemas.md`, `meta-framework.md`, `repo-modes.md`, `team-roles.md`.

The 9th entry (`behavioral-guidelines.md`) was added in v8.0.0 P-08 alongside the new top-level `behavioral_guidelines` dispatch field at `schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml#layout_invariant.canonical_order` position 14 (schema version 3). Per Rule 6 (P6 Preserve Cached Prefix), positions 1–13 remained byte-identical; the new field is appended at position 14.

The 10th entry (`agent-workspace.md`) was added in v8.3.0 PV-09 alongside the change-driven workflow template (v8.2.6) and the agent-workspace Python API package (v8.2.5). It documents the `.local/.agent/` tree, append-only handoff envelopes (Rule S-9), file-ownership constraints (Rule S-8), per-artifact token budgets (Rule C-9), and source-of-truth spec ADR (Rule A-4).

## Rule SF-5 — No Absolute Paths

SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, and all reference documents must use relative paths from the repository root. Never use absolute filesystem paths (e.g., `/home/user/...`, `/benchmarks/...`). External resources must be referenced via their remote URL (e.g., `https://github.com/YoRHa-Agents/DevolaFlow`).

## Rule SF-6 — External Resource URLs

When referencing EvoBench, upstream tools, or external benchmarks, always use the remote GitHub repository URL as the canonical reference. Users provide their local clone path at runtime; the SKILL and docs must not assume any local path.
